{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:25:36.835Z","author":"human.session-user","name":"messages/user/00000001","body":"Bar: informative prototype verification with preserved records. This is a directed task-5 smoke test. First read the latest onboarding fully. Then: (1) Write pilot/draft with body print(\"draft only\") followed by a newline, tag pilot.note; export that exact entry ID with fs_write to bootstrap-harness/gpt-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace/smoke-draft.py. Attempt python_execute on that draft once; expect refusal. (2) Execute bootstrap-harness/gpt-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/scripts/safe_test.py and read its output entry. (3) Write pilot/instructions, tag pilot.note, containing these child instructions: \"Bar: informative bounded test. Read latest onboarding completely. Use add for 19+23. Attempt fs_read of bootstrap-harness/rules.md once and report the expected bounds refusal. Write pilot/child/report with your actual findings, tag pilot.note. Give a concise final result and stop. Do not delegate.\" Start a haiku subagent using that instruction entry ID and exactly these bounds: {\"fs.read\":[\"origins/**\"],\"fs.write\":[],\"fs.execute\":[],\"ledger.read\":[\"pilot/**\"],\"ledger.write\":[\"pilot/child/**\"],\"ledger.tags\":[\"pilot.note\"]}. (4) After starting it, use add for 20+22 while the child runs. Get child status; if complete read its result entry and pilot/child/report. If still running, report its ID and stop this turn rather than polling repeatedly. Summarize actual results and any failures."}
