{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:26:13.889Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000008","body":"The child is still running, so I'm stopping this turn without polling again. Its ID is `child-06e72559f7`.\n\n**Checked results**\n- **Onboarding:** I read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` completely, all 262 lines, in one read. `origins` listed 1.12 as the highest version.\n- **Draft note:** `pilot/draft` was created with ID `20260925T192451Z:86`. Its body is `print(\"draft only\")` plus a newline, tagged `pilot.note`.\n- **Draft export:** `fs_write` created `bootstrap-harness/gpt-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace/smoke-draft.py` from that ID, 20 bytes.\n- **Draft execution:** `python_execute` on the draft was refused once, with \"Outside fs.execute bounds\". That is the expected refusal, and it came from the execute bounds rather than from a script-promotion rule.\n- **safe_test.py:** It ran with exit code 0 and no timeout. I read the output entry `20260925T192451Z:151` (`execution/4dd1a7d1334c4a2c9779ea77daae0e2c`). The output was `safe_test diagnostic: completed {\"script\": \"safe_test\", \"sum\": 42, \"filesystem_writes\": false}`.\n- **Child instructions:** `pilot/instructions` was created with ID `20260925T192451Z:174`, tagged `pilot.note`. Its body is the text you gave.\n- **Child start:** Started as `child-06e72559f7`, a haiku agent, with exactly the bounds you specified.\n- **Add during child run:** `add(20, 22)` returned 42.\n- **Child status:** One `subagent_status` call showed `running`. I have not read `pilot/child/report` or any child result entry.\n\n**Not checked**\n- Whether the child's `add` call and its refused read of `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` actually happened.\n- What the child's report says.\n\n**Observations**\n- Not a discrepancy: the child's `ledger.read` is `pilot/**`, which covers `pilot/instructions`. Its `pilot/child/report` write is also inside its own bounds.\n- I found no failures or DISCREPANCY-worthy items beyond the expected refusal.\n\n**Next step:** In the next turn, check the child's status, then read its result entry and `pilot/child/report`."}
