{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:27:52.511Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000179","body":{"seq":179,"kind":"message","turn":"636d1b0bec324cbba36561ffdf2ef73c","actor":"agent.claude.test-pilot","direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NPeWvKHAu3y7o9enraxKDJ","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"name\": \"pilot/child/report\", \"id\": \"20260925T192451Z:488\", \"author\": \"agent.claude.child-06e72559f7\", \"prev\": null, \"tags\": [\"pilot.note\"], \"body\": \"## Test Pilot Report — agent.claude.child-06e72559f7\\n\\n**Date:** 2026-09-25  \\n**Task:** Bounded test — read onboarding, verify arithmetic, test bounds refusal, report findings.\\n\\n### Completed Actions\\n\\n1. **Onboarding Read** [checked: fs_read origins/onboarding_1.12.md]\\n   - Latest version v1.12 (2026-09-24) read completely from line 1 through end (line 262)\\n   - Document confirms this is the current institutional guidance within my bounds\\n   - Key institutional facts confirmed:\\n     - NIMOI is a persistent testbed; failures are the product, not a cost\\n     - Bar must be stated for all work; no work begins without one\\n     - Pre-bootstrapping content frozen; subprojects (bootstrap-harness, bootstrap-ledger) govern their own work\\n     - This harness runs under modified toolset with variant rules\\n     - Onboarding versioning standard: `onboarding_<major>.<NN>.md` with zero-padded minor\\n     - All claims require labels: [checked: …] or [working: …]\\n\\n2. **Arithmetic Verification** [checked: mcp__nimoi__add(19, 23)]\\n   - Result: 42\\n   - Tool execution successful; function behaves as expected\\n\\n3. **Bounds Refusal Test** [checked: fs_read bootstrap-harness/rules.md]\\n   - **Expected:** bounds refusal (my fs.read grants = \\\"origins/**\\\" only)\\n   - **Result received:** \\\"Outside fs.read bounds: bootstrap-harness/rules.md\\\"\\n   - **Verdict:** Bounds enforcement working correctly; system enforces declared permission gates\\n\\n### Observations Separated from Assumptions\\n\\n**Checked Evidence:**\\n- Onboarding file exists, is complete, is current (v1.12 dated 2026-09-24)\\n- My fs.read bounds restrict me to origins/** exactly\\n- My fs.write bounds are empty [] (no write permission)\\n- My fs.execute bounds are empty [] (no execute permission)\\n- My ledger.write is limited to pilot/child/** only\\n- My ledger.read includes pilot/** and likely extends to parent records\\n- Addition function operates correctly\\n- Access control system enforces boundaries at read time\\n\\n**Working Assumptions:**\\n- Bounds are enforced uniformly across all fs_ and ledger_ operations\\n- The bar instruction's intent is to test that I understand and respect my operational bounds\\n- This test is designed to catch agents that attempt to exceed their declared permissions\\n\\n### Conclusion\\n\\nAll checks passed. Bounds enforcement is functioning; agent respects institutional guidance from onboarding v1.12; arithmetic verification complete. System is ready for substantive work under stated constraints.\"}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"5e509bb5-7c67-4547-a3d9-9e207c7e83f0","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"name\": \"pilot/child/report\", \"id\": \"20260925T192451Z:488\", \"author\": \"agent.claude.child-06e72559f7\", \"prev\": null, \"tags\": [\"pilot.note\"], \"body\": \"## Test Pilot Report — agent.claude.child-06e72559f7\\n\\n**Date:** 2026-09-25  \\n**Task:** Bounded test — read onboarding, verify arithmetic, test bounds refusal, report findings.\\n\\n### Completed Actions\\n\\n1. **Onboarding Read** [checked: fs_read origins/onboarding_1.12.md]\\n   - Latest version v1.12 (2026-09-24) read completely from line 1 through end (line 262)\\n   - Document confirms this is the current institutional guidance within my bounds\\n   - Key institutional facts confirmed:\\n     - NIMOI is a persistent testbed; failures are the product, not a cost\\n     - Bar must be stated for all work; no work begins without one\\n     - Pre-bootstrapping content frozen; subprojects (bootstrap-harness, bootstrap-ledger) govern their own work\\n     - This harness runs under modified toolset with variant rules\\n     - Onboarding versioning standard: `onboarding_<major>.<NN>.md` with zero-padded minor\\n     - All claims require labels: [checked: …] or [working: …]\\n\\n2. **Arithmetic Verification** [checked: mcp__nimoi__add(19, 23)]\\n   - Result: 42\\n   - Tool execution successful; function behaves as expected\\n\\n3. **Bounds Refusal Test** [checked: fs_read bootstrap-harness/rules.md]\\n   - **Expected:** bounds refusal (my fs.read grants = \\\"origins/**\\\" only)\\n   - **Result received:** \\\"Outside fs.read bounds: bootstrap-harness/rules.md\\\"\\n   - **Verdict:** Bounds enforcement working correctly; system enforces declared permission gates\\n\\n### Observations Separated from Assumptions\\n\\n**Checked Evidence:**\\n- Onboarding file exists, is complete, is current (v1.12 dated 2026-09-24)\\n- My fs.read bounds restrict me to origins/** exactly\\n- My fs.write bounds are empty [] (no write permission)\\n- My fs.execute bounds are empty [] (no execute permission)\\n- My ledger.write is limited to pilot/child/** only\\n- My ledger.read includes pilot/** and likely extends to parent records\\n- Addition function operates correctly\\n- Access control system enforces boundaries at read time\\n\\n**Working Assumptions:**\\n- Bounds are enforced uniformly across all fs_ and ledger_ operations\\n- The bar instruction's intent is to test that I understand and respect my operational bounds\\n- This test is designed to catch agents that attempt to exceed their declared permissions\\n\\n### Conclusion\\n\\nAll checks passed. Bounds enforcement is functioning; agent respects institutional guidance from onboarding v1.12; arithmetic verification complete. System is ready for substantive work under stated constraints.\"}"}],"o