{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:28:03.549Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000011","body":"The child completed, and its result and report both match what I asked it to do. Parent and child ran under distinct authors.\n\n**Checked, from the ledger and status reads**\n- **Status:** `child-06e72559f7` reported `completed` on a single check, with result entry `agents/child-06e72559f7/result` (ID `20260925T192451Z:520`).\n- **Result entry:**\n  - Its author is `agent.claude.child-06e72559f7` and its tag is `agent.result`.\n  - It states that onboarding v1.12 was read through line 262, that 19+23 = 42, and that the read of `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` was refused.\n  - It also says the report was written as ID `20260925T192451Z:488`.\n- **`pilot/child/report`:**\n  - The ID is `20260925T192451Z:488`, the author is `agent.claude.child-06e72559f7`, and the tag is `pilot.note`.\n  - It quotes the refusal as \"Outside fs.read bounds: bootstrap-harness/rules.md\".\n  - It separates checked evidence from working assumptions, and it uses `[checked: …]` labels as onboarding asks.\n  - It has no `prev`, so it was a new entry.\n- **Bounds:** The returned bounds are exactly what I passed in. The report's own account of its bounds is consistent with them.\n- **Identities:**\n  - The parent is `agent.claude.test-pilot`, the author of `pilot/draft` (`…:86`) and `pilot/instructions` (`…:174`).\n  - The child is `agent.claude.child-06e72559f7`, and the agent ID matches its author suffix.\n  - The parent-side status shows `parent: agent.claude.test-pilot`, so the harness records the lineage.\n  - The child's writes landed under `pilot/child/**`, inside its bound.\n  - The harness assigned different authors to the two sessions.\n\n**Not independently checked**\n- The child's tool calls themselves. I have no call log, so the `add` result and the refusal are known only from its own report. They are consistent with my own `add` result (42) and with its bounds, which exclude `bootstrap-harness/**`.\n- Whether the child read all 262 lines. Its claim of lines 1–262 is plausible, but I did not verify it.\n\n**Minor observations, none of them failures**\n- The report says the child's `ledger.read` \"likely extends to parent records\". That was a hedged guess, and its actual grant is `pilot/**`.\n- The result entry's narrative is chatty and has no `[checked]` labels. The report is the better-labelled record.\n- The report's closing line, \"System is ready for substantive work\", goes beyond what a smoke test shows.\n\nNo new child was started and no script was run this turn."}
